<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Variance and standard deviation of ungrouped data</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(c=0)"]]The numbers of passengers on {@n@} matatu trips on Thika Road were[[elif test="is(c=1)"]]A learner's marks out of 30 in {@n@} short tests were[[else]]The numbers of litres of milk sold at a kiosk on {@n@} days were[[/if]]</p><p style="text-align:center;">{@xstr@}</p><p>Divide by \(n\), the number of values.</p><p>(a) Find the mean, \(\bar{x}\).</p><div>\(\bar{x} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the variance, \(\sigma^2\), correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div>\(\sigma^2 =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the standard deviation, \(\sigma\), correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div>\(\sigma =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The deviations from the mean always add to zero, so we square them. The variance is the mean of the squared deviations from the mean, and the standard deviation is the square root of the variance, in the units of the data.</p><p>(a) \(\bar{x} = \dfrac{\Sigma x}{n} = \dfrac{ {@n*mn@} }{ {@n@} } = {@mn@}\).</p><p>(b) By deviations: the values of \(x - \bar{x}\) are {@simplode(map(string,dv),", ")@}, and their squares add to \(\Sigma (x - \bar{x})^2 = {@S@}\). So\[\sigma^2 = \frac{\Sigma (x - \bar{x})^2}{n} = \frac{ {@S@} }{ {@n@} } \approx {@vrd@}\]Or by the second form: \(\Sigma x^2 = {@Sx2@}\), so \(\sigma^2 = \dfrac{ {@Sx2@} }{ {@n@} } - {@mn@}^2\), the same value.</p><p>(c) \(\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2} \approx {@sdd@}\). Use the unrounded variance when you take the square root.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: variance and SD of a small set by definition. prt1 (the mean) has no diagnostic node: no specific misconception is plausible for the whole-number mean of a short list. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Statistics 1, chapter 2, section B, B7. */
dl: [[24,28,14,27,27],[6,19,10,18,15,16],[18,26,19,12,20],[12,25,18,21,21,17],[27,9,10,13,11,29,18,11],[23,8,7,29,21,26],[10,19,15,9,24,26,29,4],[26,5,5,12,21,23,25,11],[22,25,12,17,9],[8,22,18,20,25,17,6,4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
c: rand(3);
xs: dl[ix];
n: length(xs);
mn: apply("+",xs)/n;
dv: makelist(xs[k]-mn,k,1,n);
S: sum(dv[k]^2,k,1,n);
Sx2: sum(xs[k]^2,k,1,n);
vr: S/n;
sdv: sqrt(vr);
xstr: simplode(map(string,xs),", ");
vrd: dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(vr)+1/2)/10^2),2);
sdd: dispdp(float(floor(10^2*(sdv)+1/2)/10^2),2);
/* diagnostics */
vn1: S/(n-1);
vnosub: Sx2/n;
mad: sum(abs(dv[k]),k,1,n)/n;
sdn1: sqrt(vn1);
sdnosub: sqrt(vnosub);
/* test values */
vr2: float(floor(10^2*(vr)+1/2)/10^2);
sd2: float(floor(10^2*(sdv)+1/2)/10^2);
vn12: float(floor(10^2*(vn1)+1/2)/10^2);
sdn12: float(floor(10^2*(sdn1)+1/2)/10^2);
vnosub2: float(floor(10^2*(vnosub)+1/2)/10^2);
sdnosub2: float(floor(10^2*(sdnosub)+1/2)/10^2);
mad2: float(floor(10^2*(mad)+1/2)/10^2);
ft2: float(floor(10^2*(sqrt(vr+2))+1/2)/10^2);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
